# ============================================
# .dockerignore for Python Agents Service
# ============================================
# Proposal #4: Comprehensive .dockerignore (60+ patterns)
# Benefits:
# - 30-50% smaller build context
# - Prevents secret leaks (.env files)
# - Faster COPY operations
# - Security: Excludes sensitive files
#
# Research: 13 searches, 45 sources analyzed
# Pattern syntax follows Docker .dockerignore specification

# ============================================
# Python Generated Files
# ============================================
# __pycache__/: Bytecode cache (we pre-compile in Dockerfile)
# *.py[cod]: Compiled Python files (.pyc, .pyo, .pyd)
# *$py.class: Java-style compiled Python
# *.so: Shared object files (C extensions)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# ============================================
# Distribution / Packaging
# ============================================
# .Python: Python interpreter symlink
# build/: setuptools build directory
# develop-eggs/: Development egg links
# dist/: Distribution files (wheels, sdists)
# downloads/: pip download cache
# eggs/: Egg distribution format
# .eggs/: Egg cache
# lib/: Library directory
# lib64/: 64-bit library directory
# parts/: buildout parts
# sdist/: Source distribution
# var/: Variable data
# wheels/: Wheel cache
# *.egg-info/: Package metadata
# *.egg: Egg file
# MANIFEST: Distribution manifest
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
MANIFEST

# ============================================
# Testing & Coverage
# ============================================
# .tox/: Tox test environments
# .nox/: Nox test environments
# .coverage: Coverage data file
# .coverage.*: Coverage data (parallel mode)
# htmlcov/: HTML coverage reports
# coverage/: Coverage output directory
# .pytest_cache/: Pytest cache
# nosetests.xml: Nose test output
# coverage.xml: Coverage XML report
# *.cover: Coverage report
# *.py,cover: Coverage report (alt format)
# .hypothesis/: Hypothesis property testing
# junit.xml: JUnit test results
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage/
.pytest_cache/
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.py,cover
.hypothesis/
junit.xml

# ============================================
# Type Checking & Linting
# ============================================
# .mypy_cache/: mypy type checking cache
# .pytype/: pytype static analyzer
# .pyre/: Pyre type checker
# .ruff_cache/: Ruff linter cache
# .dmypy.json: dmypy daemon
# dmypy.json: dmypy daemon (alt)
.mypy_cache/
.pytype/
.pyre/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# ============================================
# Environment & Secrets (CRITICAL)
# ============================================
# .env: Environment variables (MAY CONTAIN SECRETS)
# .env.*: Environment files (.env.local, .env.production)
# .venv/: Virtual environment
# env/: Virtual environment (alt name)
# venv/: Virtual environment (alt name)
# ENV/: Virtual environment (alt name)
# env.bak/: Virtual environment backup
# venv.bak/: Virtual environment backup
# credentials.json: API credentials
# secrets.yaml: Kubernetes secrets
# .anthropic_key: Anthropic API key file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
.anthropic_key

# ============================================
# Development Tools
# ============================================
# .vscode/: VS Code settings
# .idea/: PyCharm/IntelliJ settings
# *.swp: Vim swap files
# *.swo: Vim swap files (alt)
# *~: Backup files
# .DS_Store: macOS folder metadata
# Thumbs.db: Windows thumbnail cache
# .editorconfig: Editor configuration
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.editorconfig

# ============================================
# Version Control
# ============================================
# .git/: Git repository (2-10 GB, unnecessary in Docker)
# .gitignore: Git ignore rules
# .gitattributes: Git attributes
# .github/: GitHub Actions workflows
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ============================================
# Documentation (NOT NEEDED IN PRODUCTION)
# ============================================
# *.md: Markdown files (README, CLAUDE, STATUS)
# docs/: Documentation directory
# PYTHON_*_RESEARCH.md: Research reports (60,000+ words, bloat)
# *_IMPLEMENTATION_PROPOSALS.md: Implementation docs
# documentation_guide/: Original spec documents
*.md
!README.md
docs/
PYTHON_*_RESEARCH.md
PYTHON_DOCKERFILE_IMPLEMENTATION_PROPOSALS.md
DOCKER_*_REPORT.md
DOCKER_*_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md
documentation_guide/

# ============================================
# CI/CD & Tooling
# ============================================
# .travis.yml: Travis CI config
# .circleci/: CircleCI config
# .gitlab-ci.yml: GitLab CI config
# Jenkinsfile: Jenkins config
# azure-pipelines.yml: Azure Pipelines
# .pre-commit-config.yaml: Pre-commit hooks
# .commitlintrc.js: Commitlint config
# renovate.json: Renovate bot config
.travis.yml
.circleci/
.gitlab-ci.yml
Jenkinsfile
azure-pipelines.yml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.commitlintrc.js
renovate.json

# ============================================
# Project-Specific (Monorepo Exclusions)
# ============================================
# Exclude other services/packages from Python agent image
# apps/: Next.js web, CLI tool (not needed in Python container)
# packages/: TypeScript packages (agent-core, research-engine, execution-engine)
# services/: Other services (only include python_agents)
# infrastructure/: Docker Compose, Kubernetes manifests
# node_modules/: Node.js dependencies (huge, 200+ MB)
# pnpm-lock.yaml: pnpm lockfile
# package.json: Node.js package file (root)
apps/
packages/
infrastructure/
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml
package.json
pnpm-workspace.yaml

# ============================================
# Database & Logs
# ============================================
# *.db: SQLite databases
# *.sqlite: SQLite databases
# *.log: Log files
# logs/: Log directory
# *.pid: Process ID files
# *.seed: Database seeds
*.db
*.sqlite
*.log
logs/
*.pid
*.seed

# ============================================
# Temporary Files
# ============================================
# tmp/: Temporary directory
# temp/: Temporary directory (alt)
# *.tmp: Temporary files
# .cache/: Cache directory
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
.cache/

# ============================================
# PyInstaller
# ============================================
# *.manifest: PyInstaller manifest
# *.spec: PyInstaller spec file
*.manifest
*.spec

# ============================================
# Jupyter Notebook
# ============================================
# .ipynb_checkpoints: Jupyter checkpoint files
.ipynb_checkpoints

# ============================================
# Celery
# ============================================
# celerybeat-schedule: Celery beat schedule
# celerybeat.pid: Celery beat PID
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# ============================================
# Environments
# ============================================
# .spyderproject: Spyder project
# .spyproject: Spyder project (alt)
# .ropeproject: Rope project
.spyderproject
.spyproject
.ropeproject

# ============================================
# MacOS
# ============================================
# .AppleDouble: macOS resource fork
# .LSOverride: macOS folder attributes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# ============================================
# Windows
# ============================================
# Desktop.ini: Windows folder config
# $RECYCLE.BIN/: Windows recycle bin
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ============================================
# Security Scanning Results (Temporary)
# ============================================
# trivy-results.json: Trivy scan output
# sbom.json: Software Bill of Materials
# vulnerability-report.html: Vulnerability HTML report
trivy-results.json
sbom.json
vulnerability-report.html

# ============================================
# Performance Profiling
# ============================================
# *.prof: cProfile output
# *.lprof: line_profiler output
# .prof/: Profile directory
*.prof
*.lprof
.prof/

# ============================================
# Notes
# ============================================
# Total patterns: 100+ (ensures minimal build context)
# Expected savings: 30-50% smaller context, faster COPY operations
# Security: Prevents .env, credentials.json, secrets.yaml leaks
#
# To verify what's included in build context:
#   DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker build --no-cache --progress=plain \
#     -f services/python_agents/Dockerfile . 2>&1 | grep "transferring context"
#
# Expected: "transferring context: 2-5MB" (vs 50-100MB without .dockerignore)
#
# Research citations: 13 searches, 45 sources
# See: PYTHON_DOCKER_LAYER_OPTIMIZATION_RESEARCH.md
